Let $V = \bigoplus_{n \geq 0} V_n$ be a vertex operator algebra over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying:
(1) the central charge of $V$ is $24$;
(2) every irreducible $V$-module is isomorphic to $V$ itself (i.e., $V$ is holomorphic / self-dual);
(3) every $V$-module is completely reducible (i.e., $V$ is rational).

The weight-one homogeneous subspace $V_1$ carries the structure of a finite-dimensional Lie algebra under the bracket $[a,b] := a_{(0)}b$ for $a,b \in V_1$.

Question: Is such a $V$ determined uniquely (up to isomorphism of vertex operator algebras) by the isomorphism type of the Lie algebra $V_1$?

